ows<br>And know the city a bit more at every stop</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="#places">Choose your destination<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div><div class="hero-footnote"><span class="tiny-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span>20 places · 7 traditions · 108 shops<br>Starting from the Takua Pa municipal brochure, then expanded with sourced research</span></div></div><div class="hero-collage"><div class="collage-ring" aria-hidden="true"></div><span class="stamp">TAKUA PA<br><strong>Takua Pa</strong><br>OLD TOWN</span><a class="postcard postcard-main" href="/en/places/tao-ming/"><img src="/assets/tao-ming.webp" alt="Tao Ming School" width="1000" height="667" loading="eager"><span><b>01 / Old buildings</b> Tao Ming School ↗</span></a><a class="postcard postcard-left" href="/en/places/guan-yu/"><img src="/assets/guan-yu.webp" alt="Guan Yu / Sin Chai Tung Shrine" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"><span>Community faith ↗</span></a><a class="postcard postcard-right" href="/en/places/khun-in/"><img src="/assets/khun-in.webp" alt="Khun In House" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"><span>A window into the past ↗</span></a><span class="collage-note">Collect stories along the way</span><span class="collage-spark" aria-hidden="true">✳</span></div></div><div class="hero-bottom"><span>Temples & Pagodas</span><i>✳</i><span>Shrine</span><i>✳</i><span>Old house</span><i>✳</i><span>Riverside market</span><a href="#start">Start reading ↓</a></div></section><nav class="quick-start" aria-label="เริ่มต้นใช้งาน"><h2 class="visually-hidden">Start Here</h2><a class="quick-card" href="/en/map/" data-qs="map"><span class="qs-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="qs-text"><b>Open Map</b><small>See what is where</small></span></a><a class="quick-card" href="/en/places/" data-qs="places"><span class="qs-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="qs-text"><b>Where to go</b><small>20 places in the old town</small></span></a><a class="quick-card" href="/en/eat/" data-qs="eat"><span class="qs-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="qs-text"><b>What to eat</b><small>108 shops in the area</small></span></a><a class="quick-card" href="/en/trip/" data-qs="trip"><span class="qs-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="qs-text"><b>Plan my trip</b><small>Save places and follow the route</small></span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav><section id="start" class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="chapter">01 / Read the town</span><h2>Start from your interests</h2></div><p>Three routes to read the city · Choose stops in your own way</p></div><div class="route-cards"><a class="route-card" href="/en/routes/#route-1"><div class="route-art"><img src="/assets/wat-boromthat.webp" alt="Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town&#x27;s relic temple)" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="route-no">01</span></div><div class="route-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Read the city through faith</span><h3>Temples and Pagodas Route</h3><span class="route-footer">6 destinations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></a><a class="route-card" href="/en/routes/#route-2"><div class="route-art"><img src="/assets/guan-yu.webp" alt="Guan Yu / Sin Chai Tung Shrine" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="route-no">02</span></div><div class="route-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Look at the story of the Chinese community</span><h3>Shrines and Vegetarian Halls Route</h3><span class="route-footer">4 destinations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></a><a class="route-card" href="/en/routes/#route-3"><div class="route-art"><img src="/assets/tao-ming.webp" alt="Tao Ming School" width="1000" height="667" loading="lazy"><span class="route-no">03</span></div><div class="route-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Trace buildings, trade, and people</span><h3>Old Buildings and Riverside Market Route</h3><span class="route-footer">6 destinations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></a><a class="route-card" href="/en/routes/#route-4"><div class="route-art"><img src="/assets/khun-in.webp" alt="Khun In House" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="route-no">04</span></div><div class="route-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Best for a half-day visit</span><h3>Short walk from wooden house</h3><span class="route-footer">4 destinations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></a></div></section><section class="section city-feed" id="city-feed"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="chapter">02 / Read the town</span><h2>City topics and news</h2></div><p>Compiled stories and the latest updates in Takua Pa</p></div><div class="city-feed-grid"><div class="cf-stories"><h3 class="cf-title">Stories of the City</h3><div class="story-tiles"><a class="story-tile story-tile-lead" href="/en/stories/city/"><span class="sc-img"><img src="/assets/riverwalk.webp" alt="" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"></span><span class="sc-body"><span class="chapter">Know the city</span><b>Takua Pa: The Town That Moved with the River</b><p>From an ancient settlement on the trans-peninsular route to a market and mining town · Verified facts and questions waiting to be answered.</p><small>6 minutes</small></span></a><a class="story-tile" href="/en/stories/architecture/"><span class="sc-img"><img src="/assets/culture-street.webp" alt="" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"></span><span class="sc-body"><span class="chapter">Old houses and architecture</span><b>Buildings built with tin money and dredger steel · Architecture that remembers the town</b><p>Read Takua Pa through the shophouses on Culture Street, Boon Sung Iron Bridge, the governor's residence, and Tao Ming School · The transition embedded in brick, mortar, and steel structures</p><small>6 minutes</small></span></a><a class="story-tile" href="/en/stories/water-trade/"><span class="sc-img"><img src="/assets/iron-bridge.webp" alt="" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"></span><span class="sc-body"><span class="chapter">Waterways and trade</span><b>From Thung Tuk to the Takua Pa River: The Day the Waterway Built the Town</b><p>The river is not just a backdrop. It is a route, a connector of people, and the determiner of the town's fate, which had to relocate due to sedimentation.</p><small>7 minutes</small></span></a><a class="story-tile" href="/en/stories/food-people/"><span class="sc-img"><img src="/assets/food-center.webp" alt="" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"></span><span class="sc-body"><span class="chapter">People and flavors</span><b>Flavours of the Baba Community and the Old Market</b><p>Food serves as both household memories and evidence of cultural exchange · Read Takua Pa through the Baba cuisine, double-layered Tao Sor, and the Culture Street</p><small>7 minutes</small></span></a><a class="story-tile" href="/en/stories/kuapapoh/"><span class="sc-img"><img src="/assets/tao-ming.webp" alt="" width="1000" height="667" loading="lazy"></span><span class="sc-body"><span class="chapter">City topics</span><b>Kuapapoh: The Day Old Houses Stand Up to Tell Their Stories</b><p>A creative space project that revived houses number 78, 109, and 305 · What the new generation tells about the town, and what history still needs to uncover</p><small>6 minutes</small></span></a></div><a class="text-link" href="/en/stories/">Read all stories ↗</a></div><div class="cf-news"><h3 class="cf-title">Latest Updates</h3><ol class="news-list" data-news-list data-news-max="4" data-news-keep="10"><li class="news-row"><span class="news-date">4/5/2569</span><span class="news-main"><b>Praying for blessings at Kue Chai Tung Shrine, Phang Nga Province</b><span class="news-meta"><a href="/en/places/kue-chai/">Kue Chai Tung Shrine</a> · NBT2HD</span><a class="news-out" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q6K2Zl6700I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read original news ↗</a></span></li><l