den="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="Your trip"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="intro"><a class="eyebrow" href="/en/">Takua Pa 101 / Old Town Guide</a><h1>One city<br>There are many more pages to tell</h1><p class="lead">The origin of Takua Pa 101 and the stories we chose to tell</p></div><div class="about-layout"><div class="about-illustration"><img src="/assets/culture-street.webp" alt="Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"><span class="chapter">TAKUA PA / PEOPLE & PLACES</span></div><article class="prose"><h2>A guide from Baan Siwara</h2><p>Takuapa 101 was created by <a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Baan Siwara</a> in Takuapa to bring together places, traditions, and shops in the town for readers to explore in sequence</p><p>Siwara Cafe is a teak house in the old market district, recognizable by its wooden gable, colored glass, and traditional old wooden doors. It stands at 53 Rat Bamrung Road. We hope this wooden house will help people get to know the town more deeply.</p><h2>Data used</h2><p>The Takuapa Municipality brochure is the source for information on 20 places, 7 traditions, and 59 shops, 86 entries in total, extracted on 6 September 2026</p><h2>Before you travel</h2><p>The source documents do not state a publication date, so the website has not verified current opening hours, admission fees, shop status, or event schedules. Contact the place or municipality to confirm details before travelling.</p><h2>The map you see</h2><p>Takuapa Municipality’s promotional map is not to scale and its distances do not match the actual area. The website uses the source map image directly and lets you zoom or scroll to read it.</p></article></div><aside class="source"><h2>Data Sources</h2><p>Compiled from<a href="https:/