t verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd>076424279 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><span class="source-offline">Visitor information sources ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><span class="source-offline">Contact information ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#gallery">Gallery</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#nearby-note"></a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>From a mining town commercial street to a stage for past stories</h3><p class="era-years">1827 to 2007 (B.E. 2370 to 2550)</p><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p>This street was not originally created as a tourist attraction. It grew within Takua Pa old town, a port and water-trade center that later prospered during the tin-mining era. Chinese people from mainland China, Penang, and Singapore came to trade and mine, and shophouses, shops, hotels, coffee shops, and service businesses lined Thanon Udom Thara and Thanon Si Takua Pa.</p><p>The buildings on both sides of the street are therefore evidence of a multicultural town, including Chinese-style shophouses and colonial-influenced buildings linked to the Baba community. The street served as the town's commercial and residential spine, not as the pedestrian street it is today.</p><p>When the walking-street project began in 2007 (B.E. 2550), through cooperation among the Tourism Authority of Thailand (TAT), Phang Nga Office, Takua Pa Town Municipality, Talat Yai Community, and Senanuch Rangsan Community, the original street was turned into a public space for telling its history and reviving the community economy under the name “Takua Pa Old Town: Telling the Past”.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://anyflip.com/yxwin/sydm/basic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">A Hundred Stories of Andaman Old Towns / Academic documents on Takua Pa old town</a> · <a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9650000044214" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Manager Online: Experiencing the atmosphere of the cultural street</a> · <a href="https://so04.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/yru_human/article/download/128497/96582/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Yala Rajabhat University Journal</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>The mining town slowed down, but the old street did not disappear</h3><p class="era-years">1957 to 2022 (B.E. 2500 to 2565)</p><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p>After mining companies closed and tin production declined, the economy of Takua Pa's old commercial district stagnated. Some buildings remained in good condition, while others deteriorated over time. Area studies indicate that the cultural street uses stories, food, local knowledge, and existing architecture as assets to bring people and income back to the district.</p><p>The project name later changed from “Takua Pa Old Town: Telling the Past” to “Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street”. The Department of Internal Trade's market registry gives 17 December 2017 (B.E. 2560) as the establishment/promotional date, while news sources place the start of activities in 2007 (B.E. 2550). These should therefore be understood as separate milestones: the start of activities and the market's registration/promotion.</p><p>In 2022 (B.E. 2565), the province and local authorities were still holding green-season activities and offering free rides on pho thong trucks. This shows that the street was being used to distribute income and draw people back to the old district. No specific evidence was found that the entire street was damaged by the 2004 tsunami or that the entire street was registered as an ancient monument.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <span class="source-offline">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce) <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span> · <a href="https://mgronline.com/travel/detail/9650000061422" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Manager Online: Opening the street during the rainy season, 2022 (B.E. 2565)</a> · <a href="https://so04.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/JSTD/article/view/254126" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Research on cultural tourism in Takua Pa</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A Sunday market that keeps the old town alive</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The Department of Internal Trade's market registration records state that Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street is on Thanon Si Takua Pa and Thanon Udom Thara. It opens on Sundays from 14:00 to 20:00, with free entry to the activities. The records identify an operator at the market-system level but do not identify a separate legal entity responsible for the street.</p><p>Today, the street still serves as a market and community learning space, with local food and sweets, basketry, handicrafts, performances, Baba dress, photo exhibitions, and street art. The old Sino-Portuguese buildings remain the main setting for activities. Some are well preserved, while others show signs of deterioration over time. No announcement of a major restoration project specifically for this street was found in the sources checked.</p><p>Archived news confirms that events continued at least in 2022 (B.E. 2565), with community activities on the street in 2024 (B.E. 2567). It can therefore be concluded that the street is still used as a cultural market and activity space for local people. Actual opening hours may change by season or according to the organizer's announcements.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/shophouse-305.webp" width="400" height="300" alt="Shophouse number 305 on the old town culture street" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Shophouse number 305 on the old town culture street<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <span class="source-offline">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce) <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span> · <a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9670000097253" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Manager Online: The 9-baht merit-making vegetarian event, 2024 (B.E. 2567)</a> · <a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9650000044214" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Manager Online: The cultural street and street art</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1827 (B.E. 2370)</p><h3>Initial development of the town and Udomthara Road area</h3><p>Old town documents classify the period from 1827 to 1897 as the town's establishment and early development phase, with Udomthara Road being one of the first settlement areas.</p><a href="https://anyflip.com/yxwin/sydm/basic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1887 (B.E. 2430)</p><h3>Shophouses influenced by Penang and Singapore ports</h3><p>Sri Takua Pa Road features Straits Settlements colonial-influenced shophouses, which are linked to trade and the Chinese community in the port cities.</p><a href="https://anyflip.com/yxwin/sydm/basic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1957 (B.E. 2500)</p><h3>Takua Pa reached the peak of the mining era</h3><p>Documents explain that the town's prosperity peaked around 1957 before the mines closed and the commercial district stagnated.</p><a href="https://anyflip.com/yxwin/sydm/basic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p class="era-years">2007 (2550)</p><h3>Cultural walking street project began</h3><p>The TAT Phang Nga Office, Takua Pa Town Municipality, and the community started 'Takua Pa Old Town, Telling the Past'.</p><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9650000044214" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p class="era-years">17 December 2017 (B.E. 2560)</p><h3>Registered and promoted as a market</h3><p>The Department of Internal Trade's registry lists 17 December 2017 as the date of the market's establishment and promotion.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">26 June to 28 August 2022 (B.E. 2565)</p><h3>Street opened during the green season with free Pho Thong buses</h3><p>The province and local partners expanded Sunday activities to stimulate off-season tourism and distribute income.</p><a href="https://mgronline.com/travel/detail/9650000061422" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">10 October 2024 (B.E. 2567)</p><h3>Merit-making and 9-Baht vegetarian food event</h3><p>The street serves as a venue for vegetarian food activities and carrying on old town community traditions, with over 200 participating shops according to news reports.</p><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9670000097253" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><section class="research-section" id="gallery"><h2>Gallery</h2><div data-gallery><div class="gallery-tabs" hidden><button type="button" data-tab="today">Present photos</button><button type="button" data-tab="archive">Historical photos</button></div><div id="gallery-today" data-panel="today"><h3>Present photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><figure class="research-photo"><a data-lightbox href="/assets/photos/shophouse-305.webp" aria-label="ขยายภาพ · ตึกแถวเลขที่ 305 บนถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า"><img src="/assets/photos/shophouse-305.webp" width="400" height="300" alt="Shophouse number 305 on the old town culture street" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Shophouse number 305 on the old town culture street<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></div><div id="gallery-archive" data-panel="archive"><h3>Historical photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><p class="muted">No images authorized for publication in this category yet</p></div></div></div></section><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Old buildings</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Sino-Portuguese houses and shophouses in the old town district.</p><a href="https://travel.kapook.com/view275997.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Local food and snacks</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Native food, traditional sweets, and local eats.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Performances and community life</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Cultural performances, local folk games, and Baba dressing.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Street art</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Art and street art depicting local ways of life.</p><a href="https://travel.kapook.com/view275997.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2024-10-10 · Manager Online</p><h3>Merit-making and 9-Baht vegetarian food event in Takua Pa old town</h3><p>Vegetarian food activities and community traditions are held on the cultural street, with a large number of participants according to news reports.</p><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9670000097253" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2022-06-26 · Manager Online</p><h3>Phang Nga opens Takua Pa walking street in the rainy season with free Pho Thong buses</h3><p>Green season activities were held every Sunday from 26 June to 28 August 2022 to distribute income to the community.</p><a href="https://mgronline.com/travel/detail/9650000061422" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2022-04-17 · Department of Internal Trade</p><h3>Takua Pa old town cultural street in the Must-See Market activity</h3><p>The Department of Internal Trade reported on activities promoting community market channels at the Takua Pa old town cultural street.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p>The activity's original name was "Takua Pa Old Town, Telling Stories of the Past" before changing to Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street.</p><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9650000044214" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Many shophouses on Sri Takuapa Road have a covered front walkway called Ngo Kha Ki, which helps shield from sun and rain.</p><a href="https://anyflip.com/yxwin/sydm/basic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Use Rat Bamrung Road into the old town, then connect to Sri Takuapa Road. The walking street section is located around Sri Takuapa and Udomthara Roads.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li><a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a> <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></li><li>Wat Na Mueang <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/riverwalk/">Takuapa Riverwalk</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/food-center/">Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center</a></li></ul></section><aside class="nearby-note"><span class="chapter">Stop nearby</span><p>Shophouse No. 53 on Thanon Rat Bamrung in the old market district is a teak house that now operates as a cafe, making it one of the few buildings on this street that visitors can enter and see inside.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://siwaracafe.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siwara Cafe · A teak house on this street ↗</a></aside><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Opening hours</summary><p>Sundays, 2:00 PM to 8:00 PM</p></details><details><summary>Admission fee</summary><p>Not verified · Free admission</p></details><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Use Rat Bamrung Road into the old town, then connect to Sri Takuapa Road. The walking street section is located around Sri Takuapa and Udomthara Roads.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>Buildings in the old town area preserve traces of Sino-Portuguese or Sino-Takua Pa architecture related to the tin mining era.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>Homes and Sino-Portuguese shophouses in the old town, local food, traditional sweets and local snacks, cultural performances, traditional games, and Baba dress</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><span class="source-offline">Open source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Database of important archaeological sites in Thailand</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Kapook Travel</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://travel.kapook.com/view275997.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Naewna</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.naewna.com/local/537042" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><span class="source-offline">Open source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">A Hundred Stories of Andaman Old Towns</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://anyflip.com/yxwin/sydm/basic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Manager Online</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9650000044214" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Manager Online</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/travel/detail/9650000061422" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Research on developing Peranakan cultural tourism routes</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://so04.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/JSTD/article/view/254126" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Kapook Travel</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://travel.kapook.com/view275997.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Postal code for this street not found directly from read sources.</li><li>Verified data on parking, restrooms, wheelchair access, and visit duration not found.</li><li>Facebook page, website, or LINE verified from read sources not found.</li><li>Verified distance from Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport not found.</li><li>Specific creators of the cultural street not found.</li><li>Evidence that the cultural street itself is registered as a historical site not found; the registration found is for the Takua Pa governor's residence wall.</li><li>Lunar calendar dates for the event not found.</li><li>Direct official image links with verifiable usage rights not found, so photos are omitted.</li><li>Direct evidence that this street was damaged by the 2004 tsunami not verified yet.</li><li>Historical site registration announcement specifying this entire street not found yet.</li><li>Documents specifying the individual founder or responsible person for the street in 2007 not found yet.</li><li>Official announcements for major restoration projects specifically for the street up to 2026 not found yet.</li><li>Old photos with clear usage rights for this street not found yet, so the photos_archive array is empty.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="Back to top">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="Quick menu"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
D:\Siwaracafeweb\output\web\takuapa101-v1\site\en\places\food-center\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Used as a starting point to explore local food in the town · Takua Pa Food Center · Lan Long Market Takua Pa · Takuapa food court"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center"><meta property="og:description" content="Used as a starting point to explore local food in the town · Takua Pa Food Center · Lan Long Market Takua Pa · Takuapa food court"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/food-center/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/food-center.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Takua Pa 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/food-center.png"><meta name="generator" content="Takua Pa 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/food-center/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "ศูนย์อาหารลานโล่งตะกั่วป่า · ตลาดลานโล่ง", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/food-center/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "ศูนย์อาหารลานโล่งตะกั่วป่า", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/food-center/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/food-center.webp", "description": "เอกสารแนะนำศูนย์อาหารที่รวมอาหารหลายประเภท", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "postalCode": "82110", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.8675924, "longitude": 98.3420033}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "มีค่าเข้าชมหรือไม่", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ข้อมูลยังไม่ยืนยัน · วงในระบุว่าไม่มีค่าเข้าชมสำหรับผู้ใหญ่และเด็ก ยังไม่มีหลักฐานยืนยันจากผู้ดูแลตลาด"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ใช้ลานพระรูปพระนารายณ์เป็นจุดสังเกต: รีวิวร้านขนมจีนป้าม่อมระบุว่าร้านอยู่บริเวณลานโล่งฝั่งตรงข้าม ข้อมูลนี้เป็นจุดสังเกตจากรีวิว ไม่ใช่เส้นทางนำทางที่ตรวจสอบแล้ว"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "วิดีโอประชาสัมพันธ์ของเทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่าที่เผยแพร่วันที่ 1 กันยายน 2567 แนะนำตลาดลานโล่งเป็นแหล่งรวมอาหารหลายประเภท หลักฐานนี้ยืนยันการประชาสัมพันธ์ในปีดังกล่าว ไม่ใช่ปีสร้างตลาด ข่าววันที่ 19 มิถุนายน 2568 กล่าวถึงแนวทางพัฒนาตลาดลานโล่งเป็นศูนย์อาหารสมัยใหม่และเพิ่มทางเลือกอาหารริมทาง เป็นการรายงานแผนพัฒนา ไม่ใช่หลักฐานว่าโครงการแล้วเสร็จ"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "เทศบาลแนะนำว่ามีข้าวราดแกงและอาหารตามสั่งให้เลือกซื้อ อาหารเส้นสองประเภทนี้ปรากฏในรายการอาหารที่เทศบาลประชาสัมพันธ์ เทศบาลระบุว่ามีตัวเลือกขนม ของหวาน และเครื่องดื่มภายในตลาด"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/food-center/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/food-center/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/food-center/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="Takua Pa 101 Home"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/food-center/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><a class="lang-switch" href="/en/places/food-center/" hreflang="en" lang="en">EN</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="Open menu"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="Search website (Press Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="Your trip"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Markets & Food</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Saved places · Markets and food</span><h1>Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center</h1><p class="english">Food Center</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">5 verified items</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="food-center">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/food-center.webp" alt="Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8675924, 98.3420033 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8675924,98.3420033" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/ui/search.html?q=%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%82%E0%B8%A5%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%87" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd>08:00 to 22:00 according to the Takua Pa Town Municipality video description published on 1 September 2024. The current schedule and holidays are not verified, and Wongnai lists another set of hours as every day 03:00 to 21:00. <span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd>Wongnai states there is no admission fee for adults and children. There is still no confirmed evidence from the market management. <span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd>Wongnai states there is parking, but does not specify the number of spots, parking fees, or accessible parking for people with disabilities. <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://www.wongnai.com/attractions/399190Vq-ตลาดลานโล่ง" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>Starting year of the open-air market is not verified yet</h3><p class="era-years"></p><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p>The available online evidence does not yet state when the open-air market was first built, who built it, or which project it began as. It is therefore not yet possible to responsibly say that this place originated in the tin-mining era, the era of the provincial rulers, or the period of modern urban expansion.</p><p>Takua Pa's context only tells us that the town has roots in trade and mining, and that the market district is an important community area. There is still no direct evidence linking this food center to a specific role in the town during those periods. Replacing the site's history with the history of the old town therefore risks creating a story that goes beyond the sources.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) · Takua Pa Old Town Boundary Demarcation Project</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>A food market that gradually became the town's dining spot</h3><p class="era-years">At least 2020 to 2025</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>A food-review source published in 2020 (B.E. 2563) identifies Ko Ek's shop as being “in Takua Pa Open-Air Market” and records it as open during the daytime. This confirms that the area was already functioning as a market with food shops at that time, not merely as an empty lot.</p><p>In 2024 (B.E. 2567), Takua Pa Town Municipality promoted the open-air market as a center for many types of food, from rice with curry, made-to-order dishes, noodles, and khanom chin to snacks and drinks. A 2025 news report discusses plans to develop it into a modern food center or food court. This is a development plan, not evidence that construction was completed. No evidence has been found that the market was affected by the 2004 tsunami, abandoned, or registered as an ancient monument.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://roijang.com/2020/05/28/dried-ricesoup-lanloang-tkp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Aroi Jung Phang Nga · Khao Tom Haeng at Ko X shop, Lan Long Market, Takua Pa</a> · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) · Lan Long Market introduction video</a> · <a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/630235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siam Rath · Lan Long Market development guidelines news</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>Still a food hub, but the status of the new project requires following up</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p>The latest evidence found confirms that Lan Loeng Market existed during 2024 to 2025 (B.E. 2567 to 2568) and indicates that small vendors were still using the area to sell food. The municipality previously gave approximate opening hours of 08:00 to 22:00, but review platforms list a different schedule, so the current hours should not be treated as verified.</p><p>No 2026 (B.E. 2569) announcement has yet been found confirming the direct administrator, building condition, facilities, or opening to visitors as a tourist attraction. There is also no confirming evidence that the plan to upgrade it into a modern food center/food court has been completed. The safest overall description is that it is a food market used by the community and small vendors, with a development direction, while current details should still be checked again with the municipality.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) · Lan Long Market introduction video</a> · <a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/630235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siam Rath · Lan Long Market development guidelines news</a> · <a href="https://mgronline.com/daily/detail/9670000105538" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MGR Online · News on raw material prices and Lan Long Market vendors</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2020 (2563 BE)</p><h3>Lan Long Market has food stalls open for service</h3><p>A review of Go Ek shop stated its location in Lan Long Market and recorded its opening hours from 11:00 to 17:00, serving as evidence of the area's use as a food market.</p><a href="https://roijang.com/2020/05/28/dried-ricesoup-lanloang-tkp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1 September 2024 (B.E. 2567)</p><h3>Municipality promotes Lan Long Market as a food hub</h3><p>Takua Pa Town Municipality recommended multiple food groups and stated the hours as 08:00 to 22:00. This evidence confirms the promotion in that year, not the market's founding year.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">19 June 2025 (B.E. 2568)</p><h3>News on guidelines to upgrade the market into a modern food center</h3><p>News reported a guideline to develop it into a modern food center and food court, increasing street food choices, but it is not verified if the construction is completed.</p><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/630235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Various main dishes</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The municipality recommends that there are curry on rice and made-to-order dishes available.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Noodles and Kanom Jeen</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>These two types of noodle dishes appear in the food list promoted by the municipality.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Desserts, sweets, and drinks</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The municipality notes that there are dessert, sweet, and drink options inside the market.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Kanom Jeen with side vegetables at Pa Mom's stall</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Reviews mention Pa Mom's Kanom Jeen stall in the open-air area, offering various curries and many side vegetables. The stall information comes from reviewers and the current menu is not verified.</p><a href="https://www.wongnai.com/reviews/c3794fae6e6d4db4bcfe9596b0bd6a2d" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2025-06-19 · Siam Rath</p><h3>Guideline to develop Lan Long Market into a modern food center</h3><p>News reported the market development plan and increased street food choices, while it is not verified if the construction is completed.</p><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/630235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2024-11-01 · MGR Online</p><h3>Coconut costs affect Hor Mok prices in Lan Long Market</h3><p>News cited an example of a Ton Pho Hor Mok vendor in Lan Long Market adjusting prices due to higher coconut costs.</p><a href="https://mgronline.com/daily/detail/9670000105538" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2024-09-01 · Takua Pa Municipality (Takua Pa Municipality)</p><h3>Municipality invites eating at Lan Long Market</h3><p>Takua Pa Town Municipality published a video recommending the market and various types of food.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The name open-air market appears in online evidence since at least 2020 from local restaurant reviews.</p><a href="https://roijang.com/2020/05/28/dried-ricesoup-lanloang-tkp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The municipality describes the market as offering savory food, desserts, sweets, and drinks, but does not state the founding year.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Use the Phra Narai monument square as a landmark; reviews of Pa Mom's Kanom Jeen stall note that it is located in the open-air area opposite the square. This information is an observation from reviews, not a verified navigation route.</p><a href="https://www.wongnai.com/reviews/c3794fae6e6d4db4bcfe9596b0bd6a2d" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Phra Narai Park <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://www.wongnai.com/attractions/399190Vq-ตลาดลานโล่ง" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/riverwalk/">Takuapa Riverwalk</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/culture-street/">Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Admission fee</summary><p>Not verified · Wongnai states that there is no admission fee for adults and children, but there is no confirmation from the market operator</p></details><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Use the Phra Narai monument square as a landmark; reviews of Pa Mom's Kanom Jeen stall note that it is located in the open-air area opposite the square. This information is an observation from reviews, not a verified navigation route.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>A promotional video from Takua Pa Municipality (Takua Pa Municipality), published on 1 September 2024 (B.E. 2567), presents Lan Loeng Market as a place offering many types of food. This evidence confirms promotion in that year, not the year the market was established. A report dated 19 June 2025 (B.E. 2568) discusses plans to develop Lan Loeng Market into a modern food court and add more street-food options. It reports a development plan, not evidence that the project was completed</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>The municipality recommends rice with curry and made-to-order dishes. These two types of noodle dishes appear in the food list promoted by the municipality. The municipality also says that snacks, desserts, and drinks are available in the market</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Takua Pa Municipality (Takua Pa Municipality) · What should we eat for lunch, and where? .. @Lan Loeng Market</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wongnai · Lan Loeng Market</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.wongnai.com/attractions/399190Vq-ตลาดลานโล่ง" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wongnai · Pa Mom Kanom Chin review</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.wongnai.com/reviews/c3794fae6e6d4db4bcfe9596b0bd6a2d" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Siam Rath · News on Takua Pa urban development plans, 19 June 2025 (B.E. 2568)</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/630235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) · Lan Long Market introduction video</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Aroi Jung Phang Nga · Khao Tom Haeng at Ko X shop, Lan Long Market, Takua Pa</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://roijang.com/2020/05/28/dried-ricesoup-lanloang-tkp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Siam Rath · Lan Long Market development guidelines news</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/630235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">MGR Online · News on raw material prices and Lan Long Market vendors</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/daily/detail/9670000105538" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) · Takua Pa Old Town Boundary Demarcation Project</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>The main Thai and English names follow the prompt; readable sources use the name open-air market. No source confirming the English name Food Center as official has been found. Search terms in both languages are suggestions for SEO, not search volume data.</li><li>No Google Maps, OpenStreetMap, Mapcarta, or Wikidata pins for the food center itself were found in verifiable sources, so individual stall or town center coordinates are not used as a substitute.</li><li>The street address, number, and subdistrict are not verified: Wongnai states Bang Nai Si subdistrict, but waterworks news search results state Takua Pa subdistrict and the content could not be accessed, so the subdistrict is left blank; the 82110 postal code is cited from Wongnai and is not verified with official sources.</li><li>Opening hours conflict: The municipality stated 08:00 to 22:00 in 2024 media, while Wongnai stated everyday 03:00 to 21:00.</li><li>No phone number, Facebook page, website, or LINE account verified as a direct channel for the food center was found, so vendor or reviewer channels are not used as substitutes.</li><li>Admission fee information is only from Wongnai, no official announcement found; current parking fees and availability are unknown.</li><li>No verified information on actively used restrooms, ramps, uneven floors, disabled restrooms, and conveniences for the elderly or wheelchairs was found.</li><li>No readable source specifies the route to the market from Phuket and Khao Lak, distance, fare, or bus schedules; landmarks from the town center are only from reviews, and full travel routes are not verified.</li><li>No construction year, creator, or founding history of the food center was found, including specific roles in the tin mining era, evidence of Chinese or Sino-Portuguese architectural styles, and historical site registration, so the old town's history is not tied to the market.</li><li>No best time to visit, duration, or dress code with location-specific evidence was found.</li><li>No regular food center festivals, event months, lunar calendar dates, or verified activities were found.</li><li>Wongnai states that Phra Narai Park is about 200 meters near the market, but does not state if it is a walking distance and does not verify pedestrian crossings, so walking time is not estimated.</li><li>An official municipality video was found, but a working still image link and usage rights have not been verified; publicly released photos or videos do not imply permission for reuse.</li><li>The food list references 2024 municipality media and reviews, not a survey of actually open vendors on the research day.</li><li>No evidence specifying the starting year, founder, land-owning agency, or reason for establishing the market was found.</li><li>No evidence directly connecting the open-air market to the tin mining era, maritime trade, Hokkien Chinese, or the governor system was found.</li><li>No evidence that the market was abandoned, changed hands, restored, or damaged by the 2004 tsunami was found.</li><li>No evidence of historical site registration or use of the location for other activities in the past was found.</li><li>The operational status, caretaker, area condition, restrooms, parking, and current opening hours in 2026 still need verification with the municipality.</li><li>No image URL with directly verifiable rights has been found yet; if photos from other pages or websites are found, permission must be requested before use when rights are unknown.</li><li>The MGR Online news date uses the 2024 context of the article, but the accessible webpage does not show the date in readable lines, so it should be double-checked before publishing.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="Back to top">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="Quick menu"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
