default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/kue-chai/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="Takua Pa 101 Home"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/kue-chai/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><a class="lang-switch" href="/en/places/kue-chai/" hreflang="en" lang="en">EN</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="Open menu"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="Search website (Press Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="Your trip"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Shrines & Vegetarian Halls</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Shrines and vegetarian halls</span><h1>Kue Chai Tung Shrine</h1><p class="english">Kue Chai Tung Shrine</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">9 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="kue-chai">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/kue-chai.webp" alt="Kue Chai Tung Shrine" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8265089587, 98.3647240165 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8265089587,98.3647240165" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd>Dress politely when entering for worship. <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://www.thairath.co.th/news/local/south/1105465" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>From Mr. Ngo Chok's house to Takua Pa's first shrine</h3><p class="era-years">No verified construction year is available; some contemporary documents state that it is nearly 200 years old</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The starting point with the clearest evidence is not a year, but a community story: Mr. Ngo Chok bought house number 87 on Sri Takua Pa Road and converted it into a shrine, driven by faith after praying for tin mining yields and fortune. Another document refers to its original name as 'Thian Wan Keng' and its legal name as 'Kue Chai Tung'.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สภาวัฒนธรรมตำบลตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Sub-district Cultural Council), Takua Pa Vegetarian Festival</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>The shrine grew with the mining town and became a community ritual space</h3><p class="era-years">No year has been found for a change of ownership, restoration, or a tsunami event specifically verified for this site</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The context of the shrine is tied to Hokkien Chinese who immigrated to mine tin in Takua Pa and brought deities from China to be enshrined. Local sources and travel media explain that the shrine is in the old market district, which has old buildings and a cultural street. It therefore serves as more than a place to pray: it is an anchor for the Chinese community and a space for the Vegetarian Festival.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a> · <a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Old Town boundary delineation project</a> · <a href="https://wanderlog.com/th/place/details/11412698/san-chao-ku-chai-tueng" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wanderlog (place information summary/user reviews)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A northern shrine still alive during the Vegetarian Festival</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The latest evidence found is NBT news published in May 2026 (2569 B.E.), which presents Kue Chai Tung Shrine, or 'Rong Phra Talat Nuea' (the northern market shrine), as a center of faith for Takua Pa people and states that it still preserves its original cultural identity. News of the 2023 festival also confirms that Kue Chai Tung Shrine participated in the Iu Keng ceremony, parading deities around the old town of Takua Pa.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q6K2Zl6700I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NBT2HD</a> · <a href="https://www.innews.news/news.php?n=48726" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Innews</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">13 to 21 October 2015 (B.E. 2558)</p><h3>Ko Teng pole raising ceremony in the Vegetarian Festival</h3><p>There is a ceremony to invite the 9 lanterns and the presiding deities of the Vegetarian Festival.</p><a href="https://www.sanook.com/news/1881366/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">23 October 2023 (พ.ศ. 2566)</p><h3>Participating in the Ew Keng street procession around the old town</h3><p>Kue Chai Tung Shrine joined Sin Chai Tung Guan Yu Shrine in the street procession ceremony during the Vegetarian Festival.</p><a href="https://www.innews.news/news.php?n=48726" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">4 May 2026 (พ.ศ. 2569)</p><h3>Appeared in NBT news as a centre of faith</h3><p>NBT news presented the shrine as Rong Phra Talat Nuea and mentioned its history of over 200 years, but did not provide the exact founding year.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q6K2Zl6700I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Mr. Ngo Chok bought a house to make a shrine</h3><p>The Cultural Council documents state that house number 87 on Sri Takua Pa Road was turned into a shrine after praying for mining yields and good fortune.</p><a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Inviting deities from China to be enshrined</h3><p>The shrine is recorded as the first shrine in Takua Pa district. It has the deity Nezha and other deities for worship.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Chinese deities</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>There is the deity Nezha and other deities for worship.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Traces of a mining community</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Community documents recount the shrine's connection to praying for good tin yields and profit.</p><a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Bridge crossing ceremony</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>During the Vegetarian Festival, there is a Koi Han ceremony (crossing a bridge to ward off bad luck) and the tying of holy thread for auspiciousness.</p><a href="https://www.thairath.co.th/news/local/south/1105465" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa old town context</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located in the cultural street and old town district of Takua Pa, which features old buildings and community arts and culture.</p><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1097396" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2026-05-04 · NBT2HD</p><h3>Praying for blessings at Kue Chai Tung Shrine, Phang Nga Province</h3><p>NBT news recommended the shrine and its role as a centre of faith for Takua Pa people.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q6K2Zl6700I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2023-10-23 · Innews</p><h3>Fierce finale! Phang Nga Vegetarian Festival procession around Takua Pa city</h3><p>Reported on the Ew Keng ceremony where Kue Chai Tung Shrine joined Sin Chai Tung Shrine.</p><a href="https://www.innews.news/news.php?n=48726" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The name 'Rong Phra Talat Nuea' (northern market shrine) is used to distinguish this shrine from Sin Chai Tung Shrine, or the southern market shrine, in the old town district.</p><a href="https://th.readme.me/p/44374" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>This shrine was originally named Thian Wan Keng, and community documents state its legal name is Kue Chai Tung.</p><a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located in the old town district of Takua Pa, on Sri Takua Pa Road. The sources read do not specify the distance or detailed route recommendations.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No readable sources have been found that specify the direct route or distance to the shrine.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No readable sources have been found that specify the direct route or distance to the shrine.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No readable sources have been found that specify the direct route or distance to the shrine.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li><a href="/en/places/guan-yu/">Guan Yu / Sin Chai Tung Shrine</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/pun-thao/">Pun Thao Kong A Shrine</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/rong-jae/">The Shrine in the Garden</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>How to dress</summary><p>Dress politely when entering for worship.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>It is the first shrine in Takua Pa District, with deities invited from China to be enshrined here. According to Cultural Council documents, Ngo Chok bought house number 87 on Thanon Si Takua Pa and turned it into a shrine after praying for good mining yields and good fortune.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>It houses Na Cha and other deities for worship. Community documents link the shrine to prayers for good ore and profitable mining. During the Vegetarian Festival, the shrine holds the Koi Han ceremony, a bridge-crossing ritual, and a sacred-thread tying ritual for good fortune.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สภาวัฒนธรรมตำบลตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Sub-district Cultural Council), Takua Pa Vegetarian Festival</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Thairath</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.thairath.co.th/news/local/south/1105465" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">TAT Media Assets</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1097396" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Takua Pa Old Town boundary delineation project</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Innews</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.innews.news/news.php?n=48726" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">NBT2HD</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q6K2Zl6700I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Trip.com Moments</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://th.trip.com/moments/detail/takua-pa-14944-125098619/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>No opening and closing times found from verifiable sources.</li><li>Verified admission fees could not be found.</li><li>No official phone number, Facebook page, website, or LINE account for the shrine found.</li><li>No postal code specific to the location found from readable sources.</li><li>No verifiable data on the exact construction year or names of builders.</li><li>No evidence found of registration as an ancient monument by the Fine Arts Department.</li><li>No verifiable data on the Sino-Portuguese or Chinese architectural style of the building itself.</li><li>No verifiable data found for parking, restrooms, ramps, or wheelchair access.</li><li>No list of nearby places with verified walking times found.</li><li>No routes or distances from Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport that specify this shrine directly found.</li><li>No specific construction year or verifiable evidence of builders other than the Mr. Ngo Chok story found.</li><li>No verifiable evidence of a change of hands, abandonment, or restoration with years found.</li><li>No evidence found that the shrine was affected by the 2004 tsunami.</li><li>No year of ancient monument registration by the Fine Arts Department found.</li><li>No information found on current caretakers, opening times, admission fees, structural condition, or recent restoration projects.</li><li>No old photos or archival photos verified to be this shrine directly found.</li><li>News from the past five years is limited; no news of restorations or awards specific to the location found.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="Back to top">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="Quick menu"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
D:\Siwaracafeweb\output\web\takuapa101-v1\site\en\places\museum\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Takua Pa Community Museum · Takua Pa Museum · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Connecting the story from old houses to the town&#x27;s memories · Wat Sena Nucharangsan · Takua Pa old town museum · Phang Nga local museum"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Takua Pa Community Museum · Takua Pa Museum"><meta property="og:description" content="Connecting the story from old houses to the town&#x27;s memories · Wat Sena Nucharangsan · Takua Pa old town museum · Phang Nga local museum"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/museum/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/museum.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Takua Pa 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/museum.png"><meta name="generator" content="Takua Pa 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/museum/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "พิพิธภัณฑ์เสนานุชรังสรรค์ชุมชนตะกั่วป่า", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/museum/"}]}, {"@context": "http