takuapa101.com/en/places/museum/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/museum/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="Takua Pa 101 Home"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/museum/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><a class="lang-switch" href="/en/places/museum/" hreflang="en" lang="en">EN</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="Open menu"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="Search website (Press Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="Your trip"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Museums</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Museum</span><h1>Takua Pa Community Museum</h1><p class="english">Takua Pa Community Museum</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">8 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="museum">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/museum.webp" alt="Takua Pa Community Museum" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8302299579, 98.3624509671 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8302299579,98.3624509671" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4412" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd>Modest attire is recommended when entering the temple grounds. <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9610000016873" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960255" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>Wat Mai Kamphaeng in a mining and port town</h3><p class="era-years">Since 1847 (B.E. 2390)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>This place began at Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan, formerly known by local residents as “Wat Mai Kamphaeng.” The temple register records its establishment in B.E. 2390 (1847), while local sources say it was built during the reign of King Rama III by Phraya Sena Nuchit (Nuch), governor of Takuapa.</p><p>At that time, Takuapa was an Andaman coastal port linking trade and tin resources. Various groups, especially workers and Chinese merchants, settled here, forming a market district and Chinese culture. The temple's Chinese-influenced ordination hall is therefore evidence of a multicultural town. For the museum seen today, no publicly available evidence identifies the year it was established or its direct founder.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.50amfh.org/userfiles/file/News/Thai%20temple%20name%20list/south/Phangnga.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Phang Nga Province temple registration report</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4412" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cultural environments for conservation (ONEP)</a> · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>From a temple and community to a museum of memories</h3><p class="era-years">No establishment year for the museum has been found; evidence shows its use in the old-town context before 2018 (B.E. 2561).</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Over time, Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan has remained a religious site and community space. Meanwhile, Takuapa changed from a centre of tin mining and trade into a historic town preserving its heritage. Academic sources describe Takuapa Community Museum as a two-storey building displaying household items, equipment, and rare objects reflecting local life, including traces of the mining era.</p><p>The temple's ordination hall is registered as an ancient monument by the Fine Arts Department, but the sources verifiable this time do not clearly state the registration year. No evidence has been found that the museum building was abandoned, underwent major restoration, or was directly affected by the 2004 tsunami (B.E. 2547), so no conclusion is made beyond the evidence.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://so05.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/parichartjournal/article/download/219292/168797/871014" target="_blank" rel="noopener">วารสารปาริชาต มหาวิทยาลัยทักษิณ (Parichart Journal, Thaksin University)</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4412" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cultural environments for conservation (ONEP)</a> · <a href="https://www.andamannlttrang.com/%E0%B8%82%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%A5/%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B9%82%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%96%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%8A%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%A3/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สารสนเทศท้องถิ่นภาคใต้ฝั่งอันดามัน (Andaman Southern Thai Local Information)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A small museum on the old town route</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Contemporary sources call this place both “Takuapa Community Museum” and “Takuapa House Museum.” It is presented in the context of the old-town cultural street, displaying photographs, artefacts, and community stories alongside Sino-Portuguese buildings and old temples. Its role is therefore more that of a place for learning about the town's memories than a large museum with full visitor services.</p><p>However, no official announcement has been found confirming opening hours, admission fees, the direct custodian, the building's latest condition, or a museum-specific restoration project in 2026 (B.E. 2569). Old-town and cultural-street activities continue at municipal and community levels, but this should not be interpreted as evidence that the museum opens every day.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <span class="source-offline">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce) <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span> · <a href="https://www.phangngapao.go.th/travel/detail/89" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Phang Nga Province: Takuapa Old Town</a> · <span class="source-offline">สถานีวิทยุกระจายเสียงแห่งประเทศไทย (Radio Thailand) <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1847 (2390 BE)</p><h3>Establishment of Wat Sena Nucharangsan</h3><p>Temple records state it was established in 1847 (2390 BE); local sources identify Phraya Senanuchit (Nuch) as the founder.</p><a href="https://www.50amfh.org/userfiles/file/News/Thai%20temple%20name%20list/south/Phangnga.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2026 (2569 BE)</p><h3>Part of old town tourism context</h3><p>Takua Pa Community Museum is mentioned as part of the old town cultural street, but no specific opening hours are announced.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Ordination hall registered as an ancient monument</h3><p>The Fine Arts Department registered the ordination hall, but the reviewed sources do not specify the year.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4412" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Community museum established in a two-story building</h3><p>Academic sources describe the building and exhibits, but the establishment year and founder are not found.</p><a href="https://so05.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/parichartjournal/article/download/219292/168797/871014" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Two-storey museum building</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The community museum is located within Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan.</p><a href="https://so05.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/parichartjournal/article/download/219292/168797/871014" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Mining-era tools and utensils</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>It houses items from the mining era and rare objects reflecting local life.</p><a href="https://so05.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/parichartjournal/article/download/219292/168797/871014" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Chinese-influenced ordination hall</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The large ordination hall features designs influenced by Chinese architecture.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4412" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa old town context</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Situated in an old town community featuring Sino-Portuguese buildings and mining heritage.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2026-03-01 · Radio Thailand</p><h3>Phang Nga hosts the 12th 'From Takola to Takua Pa' event</h3><p>The event promotes Takua Pa old town tourism, linking to local lifestyle learning and community economy, but the news does not directly confirm activities inside the museum.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2024-08-28 · Government Public Relations Department</p><h3>Tracing the legend of Takola to the charm of Takua Pa old town</h3><p>Phang Nga province and the municipality promote old town tourism and stimulate the community economy. No specific mention of museum restoration.</p><a href="https://www.prd.go.th/th/content/category/detail/id/2040/iid/319567" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan was formerly known as "Wat Mai Kamphaeng", and its ordination hall was influenced by Chinese architecture.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4412" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The Takua Pa Community Museum is a two-storey building that houses utensils from the tin-mining era.</p><a href="https://so05.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/parichartjournal/article/download/219292/168797/871014" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Sin Chai Tung Shrine <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://mapcarta.com/N7619565714" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/kue-chai/">Kue Chai Tung Shrine</a> <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></li><li><a href="/en/places/khun-in/">Khun In House</a> <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></li><li><a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a> <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>How to dress</summary><p>Modest attire is recommended when entering the temple grounds.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>Takuapa Community Museum is a two-storey building inside Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan. It collects household items and equipment reflecting life in Takuapa, including objects from the mining era. Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan was built by Phraya Sena Nuchit (Nuch), and its ordination hall shows Chinese architectural influence.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>The community museum is inside Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan. It preserves mining-era objects and rare items reflecting local life. The large ordination hall is influenced by Chinese architecture.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Cultural environments for conservation (ONEP)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4412" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">วารสารปาริชาต มหาวิทยาลัยทักษิณ (Parichart Journal, Thaksin University)</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://so05.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/parichartjournal/article/download/219292/168797/871014" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Community database, Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Mapcarta / OpenStreetMap</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mapcarta.com/N7619565714" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Phang Nga Province temple registration report</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.50amfh.org/userfiles/file/News/Thai%20temple%20name%20list/south/Phangnga.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Department of Archaeology, Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">MGR Online</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9610000016873" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สารสนเทศท้องถิ่นภาคใต้ฝั่งอันดามัน (Andaman Southern Thai Local Information)</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.andamannlttrang.com/%E0%B8%82%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%A5/%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B9%82%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%96%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%8A%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%A3/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><span class="source-offline">Open source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สถานีวิทยุกระจายเสียงแห่งประเทศไทย (Radio Thailand)</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><span class="source-offline">Open source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Direct opening hours for the museum could not be found.</li><li>Verified admission fees for the museum could not be found.</li><li>Direct phone numbers, Facebook pages, websites, or LINE accounts for the museum could not be found.</li><li>Distances and routes from Takua Pa town centre, Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport could not be found.</li><li>Verified information on the establishment year, founder, and registration details of the museum building itself could not be found.</li><li>Verified information on parking, restrooms, or wheelchair accessibility could not be found.</li><li>A verified duration for visits could not be found.</li><li>Details regarding specific museum activities in 2026 CE have not been found.</li><li>Evidence confirming the museum was abandoned, changed hands, or directly affected by the 2004 CE tsunami has not been found.</li><li>Official image links with verified usage rights could not be found.</li><li>No direct custodian, opening hours, admission fees, or announcement confirming that it remains open to visitors in 2026 (B.E. 2569) has been found.</li><li>No news from the past five years mentioning restoration or a museum-specific project has been found.</li><li>No verified image URL has been found that can be clearly identified as showing the museum itself, so photos_archive and photos_current are left as empty arrays.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="Back to top">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="Quick menu"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></b