/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/riverwalk/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><a class="lang-switch" href="/en/places/riverwalk/" hreflang="en" lang="en">EN</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="Open menu"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="Search website (Press Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="Your trip"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Markets & Food</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Saved places · Markets and food</span><h1>Takuapa Riverwalk</h1><p class="english">Takuapa Riverwalk</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">9 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="riverwalk">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" width="264" height="282" alt="Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing" loading="eager"><figcaption>Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.87157, 98.35091 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.87157,98.35091" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W816145865" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd>Saturdays, 3:00 PM to 8:00 PM <span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd>Free admission <span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><span class="source-offline">Visitor information sources ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span><a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://wanderlog.com/place/details/11412806/takuapa-river-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#gallery">Gallery</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#nearby-note"></a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>From a mining town port to a riverside market space</h3><p class="era-years">No founding year has been found for the present market; old-town context: 1782 to the early 20th Buddhist century</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Available evidence describes the history of the Takua Pa town area and the pier, rather than specifying the exact origin of this riverside market. Takua Pa has been a port town and a centre for goods exchange since ancient times, before growing from tin mining and water trade. The old town is situated in a location surrounded by rivers on three sides, making it suitable for navigation, trade, and town defence.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" width="264" height="282" alt="Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a> · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Talat Yai Community</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>When mining slowed, the pier became a memory and was then revived</h3><p class="era-years">Around the 1970s to 2019 (B.E. 2520 to 2562)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>In the later period, the area was revitalised in the form of a community market under the name "Takuapa Riverwalk Ruamjai Pracharat". A Department of Internal Trade document with data as of 31 January 2019 (2562 BE) specified its location next to Wat Yan Yao (a local temple) and opening hours on Saturdays from 15:00 to 20:00. Evidence has not verified if the market was directly impacted by the 2004 tsunami or registered as a historical site under the market's name.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" width="264" height="282" alt="Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <span class="source-offline">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce) <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A Saturday canal side market that brings old town memories back to life</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p>The market is located in the old town landscape featuring Chinese and Sino-Portuguese buildings. Riverside activities by the municipality still appear in planning documents, such as almsgiving along the river next to Wat Nikornwararam (Wat Yan Yao), and the Ministry of Culture lists a seafood festival specifying the market as the venue. However, the name of the agency or person directly managing the market has not been verified, nor have permanent restoration projects for the market itself in 2026.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gplace</a> · <a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Thai-tour</a> · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_strategy/2022-12_231dcd9d5169573.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Town Municipality: Development Plan Monitoring Report</a> · <a href="https://calendar.m-culture.go.th/events/103651" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ปฏิทินวัฒนธรรม กระทรวงวัฒนธรรม (Cultural Calendar, Ministry of Culture)</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1809 (พ.ศ. 2352)</p><h3>Original town destroyed by the Burmese and people migrated</h3><p>The original Takua Pa town was destroyed and abandoned before being revived around Ban Talat Yai during the reign of King Rama III.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2018 (พ.ศ. 2561)</p><h3>Market listed in the Must-See Market project</h3><p>Government documents name the Takua Pa Riverside Market, Ruam Jai Pracharath in Phang Nga province.</p><a href="https://einspection.moc.go.th/th/file/get/file/20210720dcb8f52155b576a7ca523b2a2247e871134559.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Information as of 31 January 2019 (พ.ศ. 2562)</p><h3>Official location and time data available</h3><p>The Department of Internal Trade states that the market is located on the canal-side road next to Wat Yan Yao and opens on Saturdays from 3:00 PM to 8:00 PM.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Takua Pa grew into a port and trade center</h3><p>The riverside area was the axis for navigation, goods exchange, and settlements of people from various nations.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Chap Se area served as an old port</h3><p>The name Chap Se is a Hokkien Chinese word meaning port, and is associated with the Chinese merchant community and the tin mining economy.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Mines gradually closed, town shifted from a mining hub to an old town</h3><p>Local historical sources note that prosperity from mining declined after the mines gradually closed, and the river became shallow due to mining sediment.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Seafood festival uses the market as a venue</h3><p>The Ministry of Culture's cultural calendar lists the Takua Pa Seafood Festival at the riverside market, although accessible pages do not clearly show the event dates.</p><a href="https://calendar.m-culture.go.th/events/103651" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><section class="research-section" id="gallery"><h2>Gallery</h2><div data-gallery><div class="gallery-tabs" hidden><button type="button" data-tab="today">Present photos</button><button type="button" data-tab="archive">Historical photos</button></div><div id="gallery-today" data-panel="today"><h3>Present photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><p class="muted">No images authorized for publication in this category yet</p></div></div><div id="gallery-archive" data-panel="archive"><h3>Historical photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><figure class="research-photo"><a data-lightbox href="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" aria-label="ขยายภาพ · ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" width="264" height="282" alt="Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></div></div></section><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Local food and snacks</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Stalls selling local sweets, native food, OTOP products, and Takua Pa's specialities.</p><a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Canal side atmosphere</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The market is located along the Takua Pa canal or river, suitable for river viewing and photography.</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Performances and music</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>User reviews indicate there is live music by students at times.</p><a href="https://wanderlog.com/place/details/11412806/takuapa-river-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Connecting to the old town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located near Takua Pa old town and the Sino-Portuguese buildings of the Talat Yai community.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The term "Chap Se" used for the old commercial district is related to a Hokkien Chinese word and the old Takua Pa pier.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Takua Pa old town has evidence of water trade with merchant ships from China and Myanmar.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Travel to the riverside area or Sri Takuapa Road near Wat Yan Yao. Sources suggest using local hired vehicles or motorcycle taxis from the Takua Pa bus terminal.</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance to the market found from readable sources</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance to the market found from readable sources</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance to the market found from readable sources</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Wat Yan Yao (Wat Nikorn Wararam) <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></li><li>Takua Pa old town / Talat Yai community <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li>Takua Pa bus terminal <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://mapcarta.com/W816145865" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/culture-street/">Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/food-center/">Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center</a></li></ul></section><aside class="nearby-note"><span class="chapter">Stop nearby</span><p>If you want to sit and rest after walking through the market, the old market area is not far away. An old wooden house on Thanon Rat Bamrung is open as a café.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://siwaracafe.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">A place to sit near the market ↗</a></aside><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Opening hours</summary><p>Not verified · Saturdays, 15:00 to 20:00</p></details><details><summary>Admission fee</summary><p>Not verified · No admission fee</p></details><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Travel to the riverside area or Sri Takuapa Road near Wat Yan Yao. Sources suggest using local hired vehicles or motorcycle taxis from the Takua Pa bus terminal.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The market is named 'Takua Pa Riverside Market, Ruam Jai Pracharath' in the Must-See Pracharath Market project and is located on the canal-side road next to Wat Yan Yao.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>Stalls sell local sweets, regional food, OTOP products, and goods from Takua Pa. The market sits beside the canal·Takua Pa River, making it suitable for riverside views and photography. User reviews say students sometimes perform live music.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><span class="source-offline">Open source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Mapcarta (OpenStreetMap data)</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W816145865" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Thai-tour</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Gplace</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Talat Yai Community</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/index.php/site/detail/4431" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wanderlog</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wanderlog.com/place/details/11412806/takuapa-river-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_strategy/2022-12_231dcd9d5169573.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ปฏิทินวัฒนธรรม กระทรวงวัฒนธรรม (Cultural Calendar, Ministry of Culture)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://calendar.m-culture.go.th/events/103651" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Muang Boran Journal</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Ministry of Commerce: Must-See Markets in Southern Thailand</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://einspection.moc.go.th/th/file/get/file/20210720dcb8f52155b576a7ca523b2a2247e871134559.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Coordinates with a specific riverside market sign were not found, so market or nearby coordinates from OpenStreetMap via Mapcarta are used.</li><li>Phone number, Facebook page, website, or official LINE of the market not found.</li><li>Evidence confirming the founding year, creator, or historical site registration of the market not found.</li><li>Verified data on parking, restrooms, access for the elderly or wheelchairs, and dress code not found.</li><li>Festivals specific to the market not verified.</li><li>Official image links with specified usage rights are not verified.</li><li>Evidence specifying the first opening year, founder, responsible person, or owner agency of the market not found.</li><li>Evidence of the market being abandoned, restored, or changing hands during any period not found.</li><li>Evidence verifying direct impact from the 2004 tsunami on the market area not found.</li><li>Evidence of the riverside market being registered as a historical site not found; registrations found belong to other elements in the old town.</li><li>Latest market opening announcement for 2026 from direct caretakers not found, so current opening days and times cannot be verified yet.</li><li>News from the past 5 years specifying direct market restoration or development projects with clear publication dates not found.</li><li>Old photos identified directly as the riverside market area not found.</li><li>All photos are links from online travel sources with unknown rights, requiring permission before use.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" ari