</script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/traditions/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/traditions/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/traditions/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="Takua Pa 101 Home"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" aria-current="page" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/traditions/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><a class="lang-switch" href="/en/traditions/" hreflang="en" lang="en">EN</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="Open menu"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="Search website (Press Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="Your trip"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="intro"><a class="eyebrow" href="/en/">Takua Pa 101 / Old Town Guide</a><h1>When the city has an appointment</h1><p class="lead">Stories of faith and traditions in the town's calendar</p></div><p class="calendar-note">Periods per original document · Not yet a confirmed schedule for the current year</p><div class="traditions-list"><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">01</span><span class="event-name">New Year's Dawn Almsgiving</span><span class="event-period">January 1</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Activities in the traditions section of the municipal brochure</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/new-year-alms/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">02</span><span class="event-name">Takua Pa Governor Worship Ceremony</span><span class="event-period">February</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/ruler-ceremony/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">03</span><span class="event-name">Relic Procession to Khao Phra Bat</span><span class="event-period">Makha Bucha Day</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/">Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town's relic temple)</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/relic-procession/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">04</span><span class="event-name">Phra Narai and Deities Worship Ceremony</span><span class="event-period">March - April</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/phra-narai/">Phra Narai Park</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/narai-ceremony/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">05</span><span class="event-name">Vegetarian Festival (Jia Kiu Ong Chai)</span><span class="event-period">1st to 9th day of the 9th Chinese lunar month · Usually September-October</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/guan-yu/">Guan Yu / Sin Chai Tung Shrine</a> · <a href="/en/places/pun-thao/">Pun Thao Kong A Shrine</a> · <a href="/en/places/kue-chai/">Kue Chai Tung Shrine</a> · <a href="/en/places/rong-jae/">The Shrine in the Garden</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/vegetarian/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">06</span><span class="event-name">Chak Phra Festival</span><span class="event-period">Day after Buddhist Lent ends</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/">Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town's relic temple)</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-khuha/">Wat Khuha Phimuk (the cave hill temple)</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-pathum/">Wat Pathum Thara (the front town temple)</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-kongkha/">Wat Kongkha Phimuk (the riverside temple)</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-nikorn/">Wat Nikornwararam</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-sena/">Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/chak-phra/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">07</span><span class="event-name">Loy Krathong</span><span class="event-period">Full moon of the 12th Thai lunar month · Document mentions November</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/riverwalk/">Takuapa Riverwalk</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/loy-krathong/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details></div><aside class="source"><h2>Data Sources</h2><p>Compiled from<a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Town Municipality brochure</a> · Data extracted September 6, 2026 (2569 BE). The document does not specify a publication date. Opening hours, shop status, and current schedules are not verified. Please check with the venue before traveling.</p></aside></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="Back to top">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="Quick menu"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
